## Analytical Significance for PRIS Research

### P3 Analytical Corpus — Core Document

**RU_079–RU_091 (13 Tier A units):**
All 13 RUs are Tier A (explicit AI/ML regulation) — the highest proportion of any document in the canonical corpus. SEBI_10 and SEBI_8 together account for all 26 Tier A units from SEBI.

**Coordination analysis relevance:**
- SEBI_10 participates in Cluster C09: Intra-SEBI AI inventory and taxonomy convergence
- RU pairs with SEBI_8: (RU_079, RU_066), (RU_080, RU_067), (RU_082, RU_069), (RU_084, RU_070), (RU_087, RU_071), (RU_091, RU_078)

### Black-Box Problem — First Acknowledgement

§2 of SEBI_10 contains the first explicit regulatory acknowledgement in India that AI/ML systems are black boxes, their behaviour cannot be easily quantified, and this creates misrepresentation risk for investor-facing products.

This is analytically significant for the Governance Debt construct — regulator acknowledges the interpretability problem but responds with inventory/reporting rather than interpretability requirement.

### Investor Protection Frame vs. Systemic Risk Frame

SEBI_10 is framed through investor protection (misrepresentation risk) while SEBI_9 is framed through compliance/management (operational governance). This dual-frame construction within SEBI reflects the beginning of investor-facing vs. operational AI governance divergence that persists in later SEBI instruments.

